## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design efficient streaming algorithms that trade precision for memory and speed when computing quantiles—a fundamental requirement in real-time monitoring systems.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming quantile estimation using fixed-bin histograms
- Memory-accuracy trade-offs in one-pass algorithms
- Update complexity O(1) per element, query complexity O(K)
- Error analysis and parameter selection (K vs accuracy)
- Comparison with exact solutions using balanced search trees

## Code Example
```javascript
class FixedBinQuantile {
  constructor(M, K) {
    this.M = M;
    this.K = K;
    this.binWidth = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(M / K));
    this.bins = new Array(K).fill(0);
    this.total = 0;
  }

  add(x) {
    const idx = Math.min(this.K - 1, Math.floor(x / this.binWidth));
    this.bins[idx]++;
    this.total++;
  }

  getPercentile(p) {
    const target = Math.ceil(p * this.total);
    let cumulative = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < this.K; i++) {
      cumulative += this.bins[i];
      if (cumulative >= target) {
        return (i + 1) * this.binWidth; // Upper bound of bin
      }
    }
    return this.M;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of streaming cardinality with bounded memory and concrete trade-offs between accuracy, memory, and speed.

## Key Concepts
- Cardinality estimation in streams
- HyperLogLog algorithm and error scaling
- Trade-offs: memory vs. accuracy vs. per-item cost

## Code Example
```javascript
class HyperLogLog {
  constructor(m) {
    this.m = m; // must be power of two
    this.registers = new Uint8Array(m);
  }
  add(item) {
    const x = BigInt("0x" + sha1(item));
    const idx = Number((x >> 64n) & BigInt(this.m - 1));
    const w = Number((x & ((1n << 64n) - 1n)) | 0n);
    const rank = this._rho(w);
    this.registers[idx] = Math.max(this.registers[idx], rank);
  }
  _rho(v) {
    let r = 1;
    while (((v >> (64 - r)) & 1) === 0 && r <= 64) r++;
    return r;
  }
  estimate() {
    // simplified estimate; actual implementation uses harmonic mean with bias corrections
    const Z = Array.from(this.registers).reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(2,-b),0);
    const alpha = this.m ? 0.7213/(1+1.079/this.m) : 0;
    return alpha * this.m * this.m / Z;
  }
}
```

